  "body": "The algorithm for setting the output bitmap currently says that if there is no ImageBitmap:\r\n\r\n> Set context's output bitmap to be transparent black with an\r\n> intrinsic width equal to the numeric value of canvas's width attribute\r\n> and an intrinsic height equal to the numeric value of canvas's height\r\n> attribute, those values being interpreted in CSS pixels.\r\n\r\nSeeing as this bitmap is not writable (you can't get another context to reference it), it seems like a waste of memory to allocate anything more than a 1x1 transparent buffer.\r\n\r\nA call to `canvas.toDataURL` would have to be ok with returning an image that isn't the same dimensions as the canvas, but I think that's still open for discussion anyway (see #3164)",
